          How to Split PDF Pages in 4 Easy Steps
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          {[
            {
              step: '1',
              title: 'Upload PDF',
              desc: 'Drag and drop your PDF into the upload box or click "Choose PDF File" to select from your device.'
            },
            {
              step: '2',
              title: 'Select Split Mode',
              desc: 'Choose "Extract Pages", "Each Page", or "By Ranges" depending on how you wish to divide the document.'
            },
            {
              step: '3',
              title: 'Input Page Numbers',
              desc: 'Specify your target page syntax (such as 1-5, 8, 12-14) in the page selection field.'
            },
            {
              step: '4',
              title: 'Download PDFs',
              desc: 'Click "Split PDF Document Now" and download your newly extracted, clean PDF files instantly.'
            }
          ].map(({ step, title, desc }) => (
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/60 space-y-2 relative">
              <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-extrabold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-950/80 rounded-md uppercase tracking-wider">
                Step {step}
              </span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">{title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Split Modes Detailed Comparison -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Understanding Split Modes: Extract Pages vs Burst vs Ranges
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Depending on your workflow requirements, our <strong>pdf split online</strong> tool provides three distinct extraction modes designed for precision:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-sm">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800/80 text-slate-900 dark:text-white border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Split Mode</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Input Example</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Output Result</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Best Use Case</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Extract Pages</td>
